1. The :ghost: icon should never, ever appear unless you've passed `--document-hidden-items` to the CLI. The fact that a documented item's consumer-visible path is a re-export of a hidden item is an implementation detail and should not appear in the docs. Also, mystery meat icons should be avoided when the reader hasn't opted into them.

2. I've also found the spot where the decision was made to ignore re-exports of hidden items: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/109697#issuecomment-1551144464

   The problem, just to summarize, is caused by namespaces. You're allowed to do this:

   ```rust
   mod internals {
       pub type MyType = ();
       #[doc(hidden)] pub const MyType: () = ();
   }
   #[doc(inline)] pub use internals::MyType as MyType2;
   ```

   Presumably, you don't want the `const` to show up, only the type.

So finally, please add a new test checking that this code works as expected:

```rust
#[doc(hidden)]
pub struct Bar;

// Should not appear.
pub use crate::Bar as A;
// Should not appear.
pub use crate::A as B;
// Should appear under the form `pub use crate::Bar as B`.
#[doc(inline)]
pub use crate::Bar as C;
```
